cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  AADMN: Adaptive Attention-based Dynamic Mesh Networks — A Graph-based
  Detection Re-scoring Approach for Crowded Scenes
message: >-
  If you reference this work, please cite it using these metadata. A BibTeX
  entry will be added upon publication of the associated manuscript.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Shafiya"
    family-names: "Kausar"
    affiliation: "aivancity school for Technology"
    
abstract: >-
  AADMN studies whether graph-based scene context improves object detection in
  crowded scenes. A lightweight YOLOv8n detector produces candidate detections;
  a graph neural network re-scoring head refines per-box confidence using a
  scene graph (11-feature nodes, k-NN edges, k=8) built from the detector's
  outputs. A controlled ablation compares uniform aggregation (GraphSAGE) with
  learned attention (GAT). Graph context improves true/false-detection
  separation accuracy by +12.54 pp over raw detector confidence; adaptive
  attention does not improve over uniform aggregation, a result supported by
  mechanistic analysis of the trained attention-weight distribution.
keywords:
  - object detection
  - graph neural networks
  - graph attention networks
  - scene graphs
  - crowd detection
  - CrowdHuman
  - detection re-scoring
  - edge deployment
